EXT. HANGING BRIDGE OF SPIDERSILK - ABOVE THE MOONLIT CHASM - NIGHT

Wind howls. A bridge of woven silver thread spans a bottomless gorge. Far below, pale lights drift like fallen stars.

QUEEN ISOLDE VANTERRE, 40s, crowned in antlers of white bone, grips the rail. Her cloak snaps in the gale. Opposite her, at the far end of the span: MORVAN THE UNMADE, ageless, a figure of black smoke and one burning eye.

QUEEN ISOLDE
You have no claim on this valley.

MORVAN
(echoing, from everywhere)
The valley has no claim on you, and yet you bleed for it.

She steps onto the bridge. Threads hum beneath her boots.

QUEEN ISOLDE
Go back to your cold hollow, Morvan.

MORVAN
Come and make me.

A horn sounds from the castle far behind her. Isolde does not turn. Smoke rolls along the silver strands.

ROYAL HERALD (V.O.)
(distant, over the wind)
Majesty! The east wall has fallen! Return at once!

QUEEN ISOLDE
(calling back)
Hold the gate!

She draws a pale sword from her belt. It blazes white. Morvan lifts a hand; the smoke thickens into a spear of shadow.

MORVAN
You cannot be in two places, little queen.

QUEEN ISOLDE
I am not in two places. I am here.

She runs. The bridge sways. The spear hurls. Her blade meets it in a burst of light, and the gorge rings like a bell.

MORVAN
Then fall here.

QUEEN ISOLDE
Not while a thread holds.

She drives forward. Smoke breaks around her. The silver strands blaze. Morvan roars.

The wind does not let up.
